/**
 * Army Fitness Test (AFT) scoring data.
 *
 * Transcribed row by row from the official "Army Fitness Test Score Tables"
 * (approved 15 May 2025, effective 1 June 2025), the file army.mil/aft links as current.
 * Every [performance, points] pair is a row printed on that chart; rows the chart marks
 * "---" for a column are left out, so the scoring rule in ../types picks the next row down.
 * Below 60 points the deadlift and push-up charts step in 10-point rows (60, 50, 40 ...),
 * exactly as printed.
 *
 * Units: deadlift in pounds, push-ups in reps, plank in seconds held, sprint-drag-carry and
 * 2-mile run in seconds (mm:ss converted). The chart's "M|C" column is both the male general
 * standard and the sex-neutral combat standard, so the combat test reuses it.
 */
